# Guard is the taunt, written exactly as samples/party writes it: while it is on somebody,
# nobody else on their side may be aimed at by the other side. It re-aims an enemy's telegraph
# with no new event and no second roll.
status "Guard"
  tags buff
  stacking none
  modify targetable of allies where source:enemies, not it.has(Guard): set 0

# The chapel's water. A curse tag, so Antiphon can wash it off by tag rather than by name.
status "Soaked"
  tags debuff, dot, curse
  stacking intensity
  on owner.turn_end:
    deal stacks to owner, ignore block
    stacks -1

# Applied to an enemy, so the enemy hits softer. `duration`, so N covers the enemy's next N turns.
status "Dread"
  tags debuff
  stacking duration
  modify damage: x60%

status "Fervour"
  tags buff
  stacking intensity
  modify damage: +stacks

# The one status that survives a battle, which is what makes it a run reward rather than a
# combat trick: `persistent`, so the tidy-up at the end of a battle leaves it alone.
status "Benediction"
  tags buff
  stacking intensity
  flags persistent
  modify damage_taken: -stacks

# What the Bell Warden's toll does to a hero: everything that hero points at becomes melee.
status "Rust"
  tags debuff
  stacking duration
  modify range: set 1

# The workaround for a relic that cannot reach a party member's cooldown: the relic hands this
# out at the start of each battle instead. Not `persistent`, so it is handed out again.
status "Quickened"
  tags buff
  stacking none
  modify cooldown: x50%

# The Tidewalker's leak, and a workaround rather than a design.
#
# What this wants to be is one line in the Tidewalker's move: `create Brine into discard to
# leader`. An enemy that creates a card creates it in *its own* discard pile, and the `to` clause
# is accepted and ignored, so the curse never reaches the player's deck and nothing says so.
# A card made by something the leader controls does land in the leader's pile, so the move applies
# this to the leader and this makes the card. See reference/FINDINGS.md #7.
status "Seeping"
  tags debuff
  stacking none
  on status_applied(Seeping, target:owner):
    create Brine into discard
  text: "Brine seeps into your deck."
